WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
There were hints that Elon Musk and Mark&nbsp;
Zuckerberg were far from best buddies

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.040
even before a SpaceX rocket blew&nbsp;
up a Facebook satellite in 2016.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.320
Facebook’s first satellite - Amos-6 - was supposed&nbsp;
to provide speedy internet to sub-Saharan Africa.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.920
But the Falcon 9 rocket that was meant
to carry the satellite into space

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.440
exploded during a test on the&nbsp;
launchpad due to an anomaly.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.840
It left Zuckerberg, who was already in Kenya,

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.560
with egg on his face. He said he was “deeply&nbsp;
disappointed” over the launch failure.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.400
Musk addressed this publicly a couple of&nbsp;
years later, tweeting: it was his “...fault

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.400
for being an idiot”. And said he had offered&nbsp;
Facebook a free launch to make up for it.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.880
The truth is they weren’t on the best of&nbsp;
terms even before the rocket exploded.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.200
In 2014, Zuckerberg had invited Musk&nbsp;
to his home in Palo Alto for dinner.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.440
They were joined by Facebook executives from&nbsp;
the company’s artificial intelligence lab.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.720
It’s believed the Facebook contingent tried to&nbsp;
convince Musk he was wrong about AI being risky.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.600
According to one of the dinner&nbsp;
guests, Musk reportedly said,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.240
“I genuinely believe this is dangerous”.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.440
He has repeatedly warned that&nbsp;
artificial intelligence could

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.280
one day outsmart humans as he&nbsp;
told tech journalist Kara Swisher.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.600
As AI gets probably much smarter than humans,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:17.120
the relative intelligence ratio is probably&nbsp;
similar to that between a person and a cat,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.160
maybe bigger. I do think we need to be&nbsp;
very careful about the advancement of AI.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.640
Musk believes artificial intelligence could&nbsp;
threaten our very existence, declaring it’s

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.600
“Potentially more dangerous than nuclear weapons”

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.840
Influential thinkers like the late Stephen&nbsp;
Hawking expressed similar concerns.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.480
But Zuckerberg has a totally different&nbsp;
view of AI. He’s far more positive.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:42.160
With AI especially, I'm really optimistic, I&nbsp;
think that people who are naysayers and kind of, try to

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:49.600
drum up these doomsday scenarios are — I just,&nbsp;
I don’t understand it. I think it’s really

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.720
negative and in some ways I actually&nbsp;
think it is pretty irresponsible.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.920
That comment appeared to be a&nbsp;
direct shot at Musk who replied:

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.400
“His understanding of the subject is limited.”

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.560
So why do they have such different outlooks? The

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.600
answer can be found in the&nbsp;
products they’ve created.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.600
Zuckerberg can’t be pessimistic as that&nbsp;
would suggest that computers are risky.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.560
And that wouldn’t bode well for any&nbsp;
company that depends on the digital

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.760
world for its very existence.&nbsp;
Facebook has grabbed even more

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.360
of the social media market share by&nbsp;
purchasing Instagram and WhatsApp.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.360
And its ambitions are growing.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.800
In October, the Facebook company&nbsp;
rebranded as Meta.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.120
Kind of like how Google became Alphabet.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.280
A clear sign that it wants to be known&nbsp;
as more than a social networking service.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.880
Meta is focused on building the metaverse: online&nbsp;
experiences projected into the physical world,

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.240
as Zuckerberg detailed during&nbsp;
Facebook’s annual Connect conference

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.760
And it has an incredibly&nbsp;
inspiring view of whatever

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.120
you find most beautiful.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.880
During that conference, Facebook&nbsp;
teased a new virtual reality headset

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.080
codenamed “Project Cambria” that’s supposed&nbsp;
to be more higher-end than its Oculus Quest.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.920
And its AI division is teaching&nbsp;
robots to feel things with their hands,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.000
to learn more about the real world.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.960
So, Zuckerberg’s personal brand depends on&nbsp;
the benefits of artificial intelligence.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.720
On the other hand, Musk’s pessimism&nbsp;
is in line with his own interests.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.920
If he believes AI-powered&nbsp;
robots are a threat to humanity,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.120
then his aggressive push to&nbsp;
colonize Mars makes sense.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.320
I cannot emphasize this enough. This&nbsp;
is the thing that we need to do.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.840
Musk’s personal brand is&nbsp;
centered around saving humanity.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.160
Whether it’s by building rockets&nbsp;
to the red planet or electric cars on Earth.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.480
At the height of the COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;
Musk defied local lockdown orders and

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.600
re-opened Tesla’s factory in Fremont, California.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.680
He called the restrictions fascist.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.640
And even threatened to move his company’s&nbsp;
headquarters out of California to Texas or Nevada.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.640
Which led to this response from Democratic&nbsp;
assemblywoman Lorena Gonzalez: F Elon Musk.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.480
By the way, Tesla is moving its&nbsp;
headquarters to the Lonestar state.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.600
Zuckerberg’s response to the&nbsp;
pandemic was the complete opposite.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.960
He said he was concerned about&nbsp;
the country opening up too soon.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.240
Facebook announced it would allow&nbsp;
all employees to work from home

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:01.360
permanently, even after the lockdown orders ended.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.200
Of course, his company has benefited from&nbsp;
people staying home. The number of Facebook

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.600
users climbed ten percent compared&nbsp;
to the same time the year before.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.160
Musk is likely not one of them.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.440
He once shared this epic meme&nbsp;
linking the U.S. Capitol riots

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.240
in January to the social networking platform.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:24.160
He also instructed his team to delete the Facebook&nbsp;
pages of SpaceX and Tesla in 2018 around

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.320
the time it was revealed that the personal&nbsp;
information of millions of Facebook users

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.040
was collected without their&nbsp;
consent by British consulting

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.040
firm Cambridge Analytica that used&nbsp;
the data for political purposes.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.600
Musk said Facebook “gave him the willies”.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.040
Zuckerberg had to testify in front of Congress&nbsp;
because of that scandal.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.240
One of many privacy issues the company has faced.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.560
Hackers breached the accounts of half&nbsp;
a billion Facebook users in 2019,

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.480
posting their names, phone numbers,&nbsp;
addresses, and emails online.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.640
Recently, the company said it will no longer&nbsp;
use its facial recognition software that

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:01.360
automatically recognizes people in photos&nbsp;
and videos and suggests users tag them.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.680
The reason given? Growing concerns over&nbsp;
how the information could be used.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.120
Public scrutiny is something&nbsp;
Musk is no stranger to.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.480
He appeared in court to address&nbsp;
shareholder accusations that Tesla

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:17.040
wasted billions buying SolarCity,&nbsp;
a company founded by his cousins.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.240
Not to mention his trouble with the SEC for&nbsp;
his infamous tweets about taking Tesla private.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.080
So there are similarities despite the&nbsp;
differences. One thing is certain:

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.840
both billionaires will remain&nbsp;
very much in the spotlight.

